WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.636
ZEKE LUNDNER: One
of the things that

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.372
spread the Camp Fire
through Paradise

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.974
was all the spot fires.

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:10.510
All those little baby trees
are what carries the fire up

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:13.346
into the crowns, and up in the
crowns, when wind's blowing,

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:17.083
that's how you get the
one-mile to two-mile spots.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.651
What we want to do in
here with our burn is,

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:21.688
we want to get it hot enough
to kill all these little baby

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:23.590
green trees.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:27.293
People's fear of fire is
preventing us from putting fire

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.029
on the ground here
in a good way,

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:34.901
in a way that will make the
people who live out here safer.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.236
But fire is not the enemy.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:41.241
ZEKE LUNDER: We're
at like 58 and--

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.512
58 and 43.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:50.917
DANNY DAVIS: Yep.

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:51.751
I'm there.

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:54.354
59 and 43.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:55.922
ZEKE LUNDER: OK.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:58.324
Danny's people have been burning
here for thousands of years,

00:00:58.391 --> 00:00:59.859
and there's still
forest, you know--

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:02.362
Well, in Hoopa, we actually
do a lot of prescribed burns

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:04.631
in a lot of our village sites.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:07.667
We don't want to kill all the
trees and scorch the land.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:12.572
You just want to manage
how many trees are growing.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:14.607
So we've been doing
it for centuries.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:24.250
ZEKE LUNDNER: The whole thing
about living in the woods

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:25.518
is figuring out a balance.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:33.226
We like to think that
we can control nature.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:35.595
Fire doesn't care what we
think, and whether it's

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:43.169
the railroad or arson or PG&amp;E or
lightning, we will have fires.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.383
There's nothing we can do
to keep that from happening.

